  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "CMake: Don't pass -fno-strict-overflow when compiling with UBSan",
  "description": "-fno-strict-overflow, by implying -fwrapv and defining signed\noverflow as wrapping with 2's complement, prevents it from being\nundefined behavior. That prevents Undefined Behavior Sanitizer\nfrom detecting it (clang since 20.1 can still detect it with\nexplicit flags, but doesn't by default.)\n\nAt least some signed integer overflow is unintended and are bugs,\nand OSS-Fuzz now tests in a way that warns about this. So if\ncompiling with UBSan, keep these as undefined so that we can detect\nthe behavior.",
